        "original_id": "bec82d10-c404-599f-a13e-6fd36a357686",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Isabella Kelly\n- Places: Cairnburgh Castle, Cairn na Burgh Mòr, Cairn na Burgh Beag, Argyll and Bute, Scotland, London, Scottish Highlands\n- Roles: novelist, poet\n- Works: The Changing Scottish Landscape\n\nFacts:\n- Isabella Kelly, née Fordyce and also known as Isabella Hedgeland, was born at Cairnburgh Castle in the Scottish Highlands, was baptised on 4 May 1759, and was a Scottish novelist and poet.\n- Cairnburgh Castle is a ruined castle located on the islands of Cairn na Burgh Mòr and Cairn na Burgh Beag in Argyll and Bute, Scotland.\n- The 1991 work The Changing Scottish Landscape described Cairnburgh Castle as \"one of the most isolated fortifications in Britain\" and \"one of the strangest.\"\n- Isabella Kelly died on 25 June 1857 in London.",
